WEBVTT

00:07.166 --> 00:08.583
[ominous music playing]

00:11.916 --> 00:13.666
[Kawaji] Ghosts of the past.

00:15.291 --> 00:16.333
[men shouting]

00:20.500 --> 00:22.958
[Kawaji] They cling
to their rotting power…

00:26.208 --> 00:28.166
and their rusting swords.

00:30.541 --> 00:32.833
Too proud to accept defeat.

00:32.916 --> 00:34.291
[Saga] Forward!

00:34.375 --> 00:36.333
[Kawaji] Too stubborn to evolve.

00:38.500 --> 00:40.958
They steal from the powerless,

00:43.500 --> 00:46.833
yet bemoan the loss
of their so-called honor.

00:48.833 --> 00:50.666
Victory is ours!

00:50.750 --> 00:53.875
[Kawaji] And like fools,
they dare to rebel.

00:55.916 --> 00:57.708
-[flare bursts]
-[man] Yeah!

00:59.625 --> 01:00.791
Sir, I see the smoke signal.

01:00.875 --> 01:02.375
It's a victory for our allies.

01:02.458 --> 01:04.208
[clamoring]

01:04.291 --> 01:05.958
Open fire.

01:07.041 --> 01:08.125
Sir?

01:08.208 --> 01:09.833
-[men shouting in distance]
-Fire.

01:09.916 --> 01:11.833
But, sir, our troops are still
inside enemy lines.

01:11.916 --> 01:13.458
I said fire!

01:16.291 --> 01:18.541
All soldiers, open fire!

01:19.875 --> 01:20.916
[cannonball whistles]

01:21.416 --> 01:22.791
[gasping]

01:24.541 --> 01:25.708
[soldier] Aim!

01:25.791 --> 01:26.750
Fire!

01:26.833 --> 01:28.333
[groaning, screaming]

01:28.416 --> 01:30.041
[melancholy music playing]

01:30.125 --> 01:33.000
Stand down! Stop it! It's over!

01:39.791 --> 01:43.416
Stand down!

01:44.166 --> 01:45.416
[breathing shakily]

01:56.458 --> 01:58.750
[Kawaji] A new era has begun.

02:00.500 --> 02:03.625
-[groans]
-And the samurai have no place in it.

02:15.083 --> 02:16.708
[dramatic music playing]

02:21.125 --> 02:22.958
These ghosts of the past…

02:26.041 --> 02:27.833
must be eradicated.

02:36.291 --> 02:39.500
Gentlemen. Sorry to keep you waiting.

02:42.458 --> 02:43.833
[dramatic music continues]

03:11.833 --> 03:13.375
[dramatic music fades]

03:16.083 --> 03:18.958
Honestly, we're the ones
who should be thanking you.

03:19.041 --> 03:21.041
This is a wonderful opportunity for us.

03:21.125 --> 03:22.541
[man 1] Indeed. [laughs]

03:22.625 --> 03:25.083
Have you heard
our family motto, perchance?

03:25.166 --> 03:27.250
No, I'm afraid I haven't.

03:27.333 --> 03:30.166
"You should never lend your money
to the shizoku."

03:30.250 --> 03:32.958
We've paid the biggest price
for their lawlessness and pride.

03:33.041 --> 03:36.083
Loan after loan, betrayal after betrayal.

03:36.166 --> 03:38.166
It's a miracle we're still here.

03:38.250 --> 03:43.375
Number 159, Ikeuchi Tekkan,
has been confirmed dead at Kuwana.

03:43.458 --> 03:46.333
Reportedly, he was killed
by number 66, Kanjiya Bukotsu.

03:46.416 --> 03:47.875
[men laughing]

03:49.291 --> 03:51.416
[man 2] Bukotsu the Savage Slasher again?

03:51.500 --> 03:53.750
-He's a beast, through and through.
-[man 1] Sure is.

03:53.833 --> 03:56.375
Yet he's all about killing
and barely moves forward.

03:56.458 --> 03:58.250
[clicks tongue] Hardly worth betting on.

03:58.333 --> 04:01.125
At this rate, he definitely won't be
the first at Chiryu, right?

04:01.208 --> 04:02.166
That's for certain.

04:02.250 --> 04:05.333
But at least he's very entertaining,
so let's hope he stays alive.

04:05.416 --> 04:07.000
-[man 2] Agreed.
-[men laugh]

04:07.083 --> 04:10.166
The Kodoku is just beginning,
which means the real fun is still ahead.

04:11.208 --> 04:12.375
There's so much more to see,

04:13.125 --> 04:16.333
and we've prepared plenty of entertainment
all the way to the finish line.

04:16.416 --> 04:19.916
So, gentlemen, may we watch and enjoy

04:20.416 --> 04:22.333
the downfall of these ghosts.

04:22.875 --> 04:23.958
[Morosawa chuckles]

04:24.041 --> 04:26.625
MITSUI BANK

04:26.708 --> 04:28.166
[tense music playing]

04:36.083 --> 04:38.000
I know that you hate guns.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.375
They cast us into oblivion.

04:41.458 --> 04:43.500
They're to blame for our demise.

04:44.916 --> 04:46.791
No one is to blame for that.

04:48.125 --> 04:50.958
The world has changed.
There's nothing we can do.

04:51.958 --> 04:53.250
Has it?

04:58.208 --> 04:59.958
Lower your guns.

05:00.041 --> 05:01.250
He needs to concentrate.

05:06.041 --> 05:07.166
[breathing heavily]

05:08.250 --> 05:09.208
[swords scraping]

05:10.125 --> 05:11.958
[dramatic music playing]

06:02.875 --> 06:04.000
[grunts]

06:09.125 --> 06:10.125
[groaning]

06:13.041 --> 06:15.083
[panting, grunting]

06:18.916 --> 06:20.208
[officer] You're in the way!

06:29.666 --> 06:30.875
[straining]

06:33.250 --> 06:34.833
-[groans]
-[blood gushing]

06:56.791 --> 06:59.416
[yelling, grunting]

07:11.666 --> 07:12.958
[breathing heavily]

07:56.125 --> 07:57.166
[grunting]

08:00.833 --> 08:03.000
-What? What happened?
-I heard gunshots!

08:08.458 --> 08:09.583
[gun fires]

08:10.583 --> 08:12.333
-Stop!
-Stop right there!

08:12.416 --> 08:14.416
-[groaning]
-The suspect has been killed!

08:15.708 --> 08:16.791
-[grunts]
-[groans]

08:18.000 --> 08:19.625
-[gun fires]
-[screams]

08:19.708 --> 08:20.708
[panting]

08:22.541 --> 08:23.500
Stop!

08:36.166 --> 08:37.708
-[groans]
-[music ends]

08:39.208 --> 08:41.625
-[straining]
-[dramatic music resumes]

08:43.250 --> 08:44.708
-[exhales]
-[breathing shakily]

08:44.791 --> 08:47.583
Get down there! Don't let him get away!

08:48.750 --> 08:49.791
[panting] Time to move!

08:50.916 --> 08:51.833
Hey, wait, but--

08:52.458 --> 08:55.375
Hey! Wait, but-- Wait!

08:55.458 --> 08:56.500
Your clothes!

08:56.583 --> 08:57.416
[music fades]

08:58.333 --> 08:59.541
[clock ticking]

09:10.083 --> 09:12.083
[brooding music playing]

09:19.375 --> 09:21.000
[breathing heavily]

09:42.166 --> 09:43.875
[grunting]

09:58.500 --> 10:01.000
Your purpose here is pointless.

10:01.083 --> 10:03.916
Even winning this game
won't make anybody happy.

10:05.208 --> 10:07.166
What are you implying?

10:07.250 --> 10:10.833
It's no use trying
to make you understand! [grunting]

10:12.541 --> 10:13.916
[struggling]

10:14.000 --> 10:16.000
[tense music playing]

10:16.083 --> 10:18.458
This is where your journey ends,

10:19.041 --> 10:21.041
Saga Kokushu.

10:21.125 --> 10:22.166
[straining]

10:33.916 --> 10:35.541
[music intensifies]

10:40.000 --> 10:41.375
[music fades]

10:41.458 --> 10:42.375
[Saga groaning]

10:42.458 --> 10:43.541
Shu-nii!

10:44.750 --> 10:45.750
-[grunts]
-[groaning]

10:48.291 --> 10:50.083
-Get them!
-[whimpering]

10:51.333 --> 10:53.041
[footsteps receding]

11:00.125 --> 11:01.125
[inhales]

11:03.958 --> 11:05.958
[ominous music playing]

11:09.666 --> 11:11.458
So we'll meet in Tokyo.

11:16.500 --> 11:17.583
[knocking]

11:17.666 --> 11:18.958
[clock ticking]

11:20.791 --> 11:21.791
Come in.

11:28.250 --> 11:30.000
We've received a report
from General Kawaji.

11:31.916 --> 11:33.791
They found nothing
at the foot of Mount Fuji.

11:33.875 --> 11:36.416
We chased a false lead, unfortunately.

11:36.500 --> 11:37.916
Thank you, Nagase.

11:38.625 --> 11:42.416
Lord Okubo,
regarding what Lord Maejima said earlier…

11:43.708 --> 11:44.750
About Kawaji?

11:44.833 --> 11:45.958
Yes.

11:46.541 --> 11:49.375
Lord Kawaji is admirable, truly.

11:49.458 --> 11:51.541
-However--
-The Bureau was his doing.

11:52.208 --> 11:54.708
Kawaji went overseas
to develop a plan for it,

11:54.791 --> 11:57.708
went to Europe
to learn new ideas for law and order.

12:00.750 --> 12:03.250
But I don't believe
he'll betray us in the end.

12:05.375 --> 12:06.375
[inhales]

12:08.458 --> 12:09.750
If you'll allow it,

12:10.708 --> 12:12.791
could I take a look
at those documents, sir?

12:14.250 --> 12:15.750
Can you decipher it?

12:15.833 --> 12:17.166
[Nagase] I'm not sure.

12:18.333 --> 12:19.791
I'll do my best.

12:20.583 --> 12:21.875
I'm no expert.

12:22.458 --> 12:24.666
However, I'd like to give it a try.

12:27.333 --> 12:28.250
Hm.

12:29.541 --> 12:31.708
[brooding music playing]

12:31.791 --> 12:32.958
Tend to every detail.

12:33.791 --> 12:36.458
We have no idea
what the enemy might be hiding.

12:36.541 --> 12:37.500
[Nagase] Thank you, sir.

12:46.541 --> 12:48.250
-[door closes]
-[exhales]

12:51.750 --> 12:55.708
The man who killed Akayama
and attacked me was no impostor.

12:55.791 --> 12:57.458
He was a real police officer.

12:58.958 --> 13:01.875
That means the Police Bureau
might actually have a connection

13:01.958 --> 13:04.041
to whoever's in charge of all this.

13:04.125 --> 13:07.166
-Or maybe--
-It's someone inside the Bureau.

13:07.250 --> 13:08.666
[Kyojin] Exactly.

13:08.750 --> 13:10.166
So the police

13:10.666 --> 13:12.291
and Mitsui Bank as well…

13:12.375 --> 13:14.875
I'd wager
it's not just the bank that's involved.

13:15.458 --> 13:16.416
I don't follow.

13:16.500 --> 13:20.000
There's a chance the zaibatsu
in charge of the banks are involved.

13:20.083 --> 13:21.000
[gasps]

13:21.083 --> 13:22.750
If that really is the case,

13:22.833 --> 13:24.750
that would explain everything,
wouldn't it?

13:25.500 --> 13:27.875
The Police Bureau
monitors the participants

13:27.958 --> 13:31.666
and sees to the disposal
of any bodies left in their wake.

13:32.458 --> 13:34.666
And as for the extensive cost
of its operation,

13:34.750 --> 13:36.708
it's all covered by the zaibatsu.

13:36.791 --> 13:38.541
[Saga] Still, one thing remains puzzling.

13:38.625 --> 13:41.958
At Tenryuji, the very first
to die was Ando Jinbe, right?

13:42.041 --> 13:44.458
He was an officer
of Kyoto's Fourth Division.

13:44.541 --> 13:45.750
[Shinnosuke] Yes, you're right!

13:45.833 --> 13:48.125
I don't think the officers
at the station knew either.

13:48.208 --> 13:51.958
So I take it only the core
of the Police Bureau is at work here.

13:53.208 --> 13:55.458
But why would the police
allow all of this?

13:55.541 --> 13:56.916
[Kyojin] I have no clue.

13:57.000 --> 14:00.875
However, there is something
I can speak to with certainty for now.

14:02.666 --> 14:05.583
This Kodoku is not only for 100,000 yen.

14:05.666 --> 14:08.583
It's obviously
about something far deeper than that.

14:09.166 --> 14:12.458
Even if we do reach Tokyo,
I doubt that will be the end of it.

14:14.250 --> 14:16.541
I'm sure
they'll have something else in store.

14:16.625 --> 14:19.791
What if they force us to kill each other
until there's only one standing?

14:19.875 --> 14:22.666
[Saga] And even if
only one person is left,

14:23.833 --> 14:26.458
there's no guarantee
they'll return home alive.

14:28.333 --> 14:30.083
No way. [breath trembling]

14:33.000 --> 14:34.291
[Saga] Even so,

14:35.791 --> 14:37.416
I'll keep moving forward.

14:39.291 --> 14:41.500
[Kyojin] Will you bring
the little miss with you?

14:45.500 --> 14:48.666
Though I suppose
there's a limit to how far she can go.

14:48.750 --> 14:49.583
[music fades]

14:49.666 --> 14:50.875
[Saga exhales]

14:54.708 --> 14:56.416
But I want to go with you. Please.

15:00.833 --> 15:02.083
Futaba…

15:04.166 --> 15:05.458
please be quiet.

15:10.791 --> 15:12.125
[footsteps approaching]

15:12.208 --> 15:15.916
And you still have a trump card
hidden up your sleeve, don't you?

15:16.000 --> 15:17.916
Saga Kokushu, sir.

15:19.666 --> 15:21.333
Back during the war, you were connected

15:21.416 --> 15:23.958
to some prominent government figures,
weren't you?

15:25.083 --> 15:27.750
How do you know
something like that, Kyojin?

15:28.416 --> 15:32.083
The zaibatsu and the police will fail
if we utilize that card.

15:35.500 --> 15:37.666
So if you care
about this little kiddo here,

15:37.750 --> 15:40.500
[exhales]
you might want to give it some thought.

15:47.708 --> 15:49.083
[breath trembling]

15:55.958 --> 15:57.041
[inhales sharply]

15:57.125 --> 15:59.083
[Saga] I'll be back by noon tomorrow.

16:00.041 --> 16:01.333
While I'm gone,

16:02.208 --> 16:03.250
take care of Futaba.

16:03.333 --> 16:04.666
[Kyojin] Understood.

16:08.291 --> 16:09.625
[breathing shakily]

16:17.791 --> 16:18.791
[breathing heavily]

16:34.750 --> 16:36.875
[Iroha] That kind
of strike won't be effective.

16:41.708 --> 16:43.458
I just want to be strong.

16:44.333 --> 16:46.125
That's why I'm doing this.

16:48.875 --> 16:50.416
I don't want to…

16:52.666 --> 16:54.916
be such a heavy burden to you all.

17:00.000 --> 17:01.291
[sobbing gently]

17:09.083 --> 17:11.583
Strength doesn't lie in the sword alone.

17:15.500 --> 17:17.416
At the moment, you're still weak.

17:18.833 --> 17:20.458
You're only a child.

17:21.250 --> 17:22.791
And you're also a girl.

17:27.791 --> 17:29.333
But prepare yourself.

17:32.750 --> 17:35.916
In time, you will find the strength
and power you truly carry.

17:44.291 --> 17:46.291
[brooding music playing]

18:01.250 --> 18:04.083
-[indistinct chatter]
-[birds chirping]

18:04.166 --> 18:07.500
NARUMI TELEGRAPH OFFICE

18:12.375 --> 18:13.375
Oh.

18:14.583 --> 18:15.750
How may I help you?

18:15.833 --> 18:18.000
I have a telegram to send.

18:18.083 --> 18:20.291
[clerk] Ah. Yes, of course.

18:20.375 --> 18:23.750
Please write the recipient's name
and the message here.

18:29.166 --> 18:31.041
[mysterious music playing]

18:31.125 --> 18:34.875
SPECIAL EXERCISE BY THE POLICE BUREAU

18:35.666 --> 18:36.666
[knocking]

18:37.375 --> 18:38.375
Come in.

18:41.750 --> 18:43.291
-If I may…
-What is it?

18:43.375 --> 18:45.250
A telegram has arrived.

18:45.333 --> 18:47.583
It's addressed to the Home Minister
and appears quite odd.

18:51.666 --> 18:53.208
WISH TO CONVEY IMPORTANT MATTER TO OKUBO

18:53.291 --> 18:54.791
[Maejima] Saga Kokushu.

18:58.958 --> 19:00.208
I have to send a telegram.

19:05.208 --> 19:06.041
I'll do it.

19:06.958 --> 19:08.583
Everyone out, all right?

19:09.916 --> 19:11.291
-Yes, sir.
-[clerk] Yes, sir.

19:11.375 --> 19:13.000
[tense music playing]

19:24.500 --> 19:26.375
All right. They've responded.

19:27.125 --> 19:28.375
What did they say?

19:28.958 --> 19:30.708
They said, "Details, please."

19:30.791 --> 19:31.833
Who sent the reply?

19:33.250 --> 19:35.000
Lord Maejima Hisoka, sir.

19:35.625 --> 19:39.125
How is this possible?
He's the Home Minister's right-hand!

19:39.958 --> 19:41.666
I'm afraid you need to leave for now.

19:43.166 --> 19:45.125
This matter doesn't concern you.

19:45.916 --> 19:47.208
[gasps] Uh, sure.

20:10.125 --> 20:11.791
[Saga] Serious incident at Tenryuji.

20:11.875 --> 20:13.791
Has it been confirmed?

20:15.583 --> 20:18.333
[Maejima] Reports received.
Shizoku assembling.

20:18.416 --> 20:19.833
Are you one of them?

20:19.916 --> 20:21.250
[Saga] I am.

20:21.875 --> 20:24.250
Shizoku engaged in combat.

20:24.333 --> 20:25.666
Child among them.

20:26.583 --> 20:27.791
Requesting assistance.

20:30.541 --> 20:32.250
[Maejima] Still investigating.

20:32.333 --> 20:34.041
Requesting full details.

20:35.375 --> 20:36.458
[exhales]

20:38.291 --> 20:39.750
[Enju] Rule four.

20:39.833 --> 20:42.500
Under no circumstances,
are you to tell anyone else about this.

20:47.500 --> 20:50.500
[Saga] Provide protection,
and details will follow.

20:51.916 --> 20:55.166
[Maejima] Police involvement is suspected.
Any knowledge?

20:56.041 --> 20:59.583
[Saga] Matter of national importance.
Will provide information if protected.

21:04.666 --> 21:06.833
[Maejima] Meet in Okazaki in three days.

21:06.916 --> 21:08.875
Protection to follow there.

21:11.125 --> 21:12.291
[Saga] Understood.

21:19.458 --> 21:20.958
[tense music fades]

21:21.041 --> 21:23.375
Sorry for the scare. I apologize.

21:24.250 --> 21:25.708
Could you send this one too?

21:25.791 --> 21:27.000
[clerk] Oh. Yes, sir.

21:31.333 --> 21:32.250
Thank you, sir.

21:33.083 --> 21:35.625
TO: SHINO SAGA
FROM: SHUJIRO SAGA

21:36.500 --> 21:38.000
[Saga] Remain strong.

21:40.916 --> 21:42.500
I will return no matter what.

21:49.125 --> 21:51.125
-[vehicles passing]
-[indistinct chatter]

21:51.208 --> 21:54.291
[Maejima] Saga Kokushu seems
to be among the participants.

21:54.375 --> 21:55.875
Kokushu, you say?

21:55.958 --> 21:57.125
[Maejima] Yes, sir.

21:57.791 --> 22:00.708
-[Okubo] So he's still alive.
-[Maejima] He asked for help.

22:00.791 --> 22:02.750
There's a child he wants to protect.

22:05.041 --> 22:06.666
Any other details?

22:07.250 --> 22:11.125
He didn't offer any clear answers
when I asked about police involvement,

22:11.208 --> 22:12.791
but said it was a national issue.

22:14.416 --> 22:15.833
And there's more, sir.

22:15.916 --> 22:20.250
The Police Bureau is mobilizing
over 150 officers

22:20.333 --> 22:22.250
and conducting exercises in secret.

22:23.333 --> 22:25.833
The way I see it,
they're likely proceeding with something

22:25.916 --> 22:28.041
and choosing not to inform us.

22:28.625 --> 22:30.333
Kawaji is able to utilize his power

22:30.416 --> 22:32.625
to command anyone
in the police force at any moment

22:32.708 --> 22:35.750
and continue his relationship
with the zaibatsu.

22:35.833 --> 22:37.833
[mysterious music playing]

22:38.833 --> 22:40.208
Lord Okubo.

22:43.208 --> 22:44.375
I will not give up.

22:45.000 --> 22:46.458
I'll do my best.

22:49.708 --> 22:53.083
As soon as Kawaji returns,
he and I will have a discussion.

22:54.500 --> 22:57.333
In the meantime,
those telegrams must be decoded.

22:57.416 --> 22:59.458
We won't catch him without any real proof.

22:59.541 --> 23:03.041
Yes, sir.
I'll be on my way to meet Kokushu myself.

23:03.125 --> 23:05.250
Please make sure you're always alert.

23:05.333 --> 23:06.333
Sir.

23:29.916 --> 23:34.041
FIREARMS - EQUIPMENT
WESTERN POLICE SYSTEM

23:34.125 --> 23:38.625
FORMATION OF A MODERN STATE POLICE

23:38.708 --> 23:40.458
TRAINING IS NECESSARY FOR EMERGENCIES

23:43.666 --> 23:45.791
[Nagase] Ru… Ru… Ru… Ru Ke…

23:45.875 --> 23:48.000
MITSUI-GUMI CODEBOOK

23:48.083 --> 23:49.083
One…

23:49.625 --> 23:50.791
Eleven…

23:51.291 --> 23:52.291
Ten…

23:53.291 --> 23:54.583
Eleven…

23:55.166 --> 23:56.250
[inhales]

23:58.250 --> 23:59.250
[sighing]

24:16.000 --> 24:17.416
[birds chirping]

24:38.500 --> 24:41.666
-[Saga] Forgive the wait.
-All right, let's get going.

24:41.750 --> 24:44.000
We're probably
at the very end of the line.

24:44.083 --> 24:47.083
Most contestants have likely passed
through Chiryu by now.

24:47.166 --> 24:50.000
We should hurry,
or there won't be any tags left to take.

24:50.083 --> 24:52.416
Right. Let's move.

24:57.291 --> 24:59.083
[foreboding music playing]

25:04.750 --> 25:09.458
SEKI

25:12.458 --> 25:15.708
CHIRYU

25:15.791 --> 25:17.750
[indistinct chatter]

25:17.833 --> 25:21.208
CHIRYU-JUKU
REQUIRED POINTS: 5

25:36.083 --> 25:38.416
Welcome, all. We've been expecting you.

25:39.083 --> 25:42.125
Mr. Saga, Miss Katsuki,
Miss Kinugasa, tags, please.

25:42.208 --> 25:45.041
[man 1] Mr. Tsuge, Mr. Sayama, your tags.

25:47.125 --> 25:48.666
[Tsurubami] Mr. Saga Shujiro,

25:48.750 --> 25:49.875
eight points.

25:49.958 --> 25:53.000
Miss Katsuki Futaba, seven points.

25:53.083 --> 25:56.083
Miss Kinugasa Iroha, eight points.

25:58.208 --> 26:00.666
You've made it to Chiryu,
and you're all cleared to pass.

26:00.750 --> 26:03.625
[man 1] Mr. Tsuge Kyojin, seven points.

26:03.708 --> 26:05.541
You are cleared to pass Chiryu.

26:07.333 --> 26:09.666
Five tags will now become one blue tag.

26:09.750 --> 26:12.416
Please hand over
five points' worth of tags.

26:13.333 --> 26:15.041
[breathing shakily]

26:22.833 --> 26:25.750
[man 2] Mr. Sayama, your tags, please.

26:34.666 --> 26:35.916
No, wait.

26:36.000 --> 26:39.833
-Futaba, let's go.
-[struggling] Shujiro, wait!

26:41.541 --> 26:44.291
-We all have enough to spare!
-There's no use in taking him with us.

26:44.375 --> 26:46.541
He lacks the strength
to survive, all right?

26:46.625 --> 26:49.125
Stop this! We have to save Shinnosuke!

26:49.958 --> 26:52.750
We're barely managing
to survive ourselves.

26:53.250 --> 26:57.208
Shinnosuke is an adult.
His life's his own to answer for.

26:57.708 --> 27:01.291
He made his choice,
and he wasn't forced into anything.

27:18.625 --> 27:19.625
[Shinnosuke] Futaba.

27:22.791 --> 27:24.000
Thank you.

27:27.875 --> 27:29.750
[somber music playing]

27:31.041 --> 27:32.458
[sobbing gently]

27:37.041 --> 27:38.375
I can't say

27:38.958 --> 27:41.125
what's going to happen from here.

27:43.875 --> 27:47.541
And I know every moment could be the last.

27:50.750 --> 27:51.708
But…

27:55.250 --> 27:57.833
But if abandoning Shinnosuke
means I survive,

27:57.916 --> 28:00.291
how could I return
to my mother with any pride?

28:01.166 --> 28:03.333
How could I ever face her again

28:04.208 --> 28:05.916
if I have no honor?

28:11.125 --> 28:12.583
[Tsurubami] There's no use.

28:12.666 --> 28:15.291
All this would do is
put off his certain death.

28:16.000 --> 28:17.958
Sayama does not have the skills.

28:18.041 --> 28:21.041
It's unlikely he'll survive until the end
and become one of the nine.

28:25.333 --> 28:27.416
What if there are more paths
to our survival?

28:27.500 --> 28:29.000
Gibberish.

28:47.625 --> 28:48.833
[breathing heavily]

28:59.291 --> 29:00.291
[sighs]

29:10.208 --> 29:11.208
[chuckles]

29:11.916 --> 29:13.791
I guess it's a done deal.

29:15.458 --> 29:16.458
[sighs]

29:21.916 --> 29:23.333
[breath trembling]

30:15.875 --> 30:18.916
[man 2] Mr. Sayama Shinnosuke,
five points.

30:19.000 --> 30:21.000
You are cleared to pass Chiryu.

30:23.750 --> 30:24.875
[Shinnosuke] Futaba.

30:25.791 --> 30:26.875
Thank you.

30:26.958 --> 30:28.666
[footsteps receding]

30:30.791 --> 30:31.875
Thank you so much!

30:31.958 --> 30:37.833
[sobbing] Thank you!
Thank you so much! Thank you!

30:46.250 --> 30:47.708
Safe travels.

30:48.708 --> 30:50.083
[birds chirping]

30:52.083 --> 30:53.500
[somber music fades]

30:53.583 --> 30:55.625
-Shujiro.
-Hm?

30:56.500 --> 30:57.750
I'm sorry.

31:00.041 --> 31:01.625
If it weren't for you,

31:01.708 --> 31:03.750
I wouldn't have made it this far.

31:04.833 --> 31:06.166
No.

31:06.250 --> 31:08.041
You were right, actually.

31:08.541 --> 31:10.458
We cannot save everybody.

31:10.958 --> 31:13.583
But abandoning the person
right in front of us,

31:13.666 --> 31:15.708
I could never face my wife again.

31:16.375 --> 31:18.750
[Kyojin] I must say,
Futaba, excellent work.

31:18.833 --> 31:20.458
[Saga] Indeed.

31:20.541 --> 31:22.583
Tsurubami has spoken carelessly.

31:23.625 --> 31:27.333
He revealed that at the game's end,
nine would stand a chance of survival.

31:29.833 --> 31:32.625
You're right.
He did say something like that.

31:33.875 --> 31:36.500
The nine who reach Tokyo
will be forced into something.

31:36.583 --> 31:38.375
I have no doubt of that.

31:38.458 --> 31:39.458
However,

31:39.541 --> 31:42.375
that is not to say
only one will survive, is it?

31:44.583 --> 31:45.916
[uplifting music playing]

31:46.000 --> 31:47.041
Yes, but

31:47.875 --> 31:52.166
he's involved in the Kodoku, so then…
why would he reveal that to us?

31:52.791 --> 31:55.958
He's definitely not on our side,
yet I'm sensing some goodwill.

31:57.583 --> 31:59.250
Not for us, exactly.

32:00.208 --> 32:01.291
For Futaba.

32:02.791 --> 32:04.000
[Kyojin] Who would've thought?

32:04.083 --> 32:07.625
If this Kodoku is like a locked door,
maybe you hold the key, huh?

32:09.875 --> 32:12.208
[Saga] There's finally hope
in this Kodoku.

32:12.916 --> 32:16.416
Futaba. It's all because of you.

32:21.291 --> 32:23.083
[footsteps receding]

32:39.708 --> 32:42.583
-[groaning]
-[people gasping, screaming]

32:44.291 --> 32:45.875
[dramatic music playing]

32:45.958 --> 32:47.333
[whimpering]

32:47.958 --> 32:50.333
[Kanjiya] So,
what were you saying about a samurai?

32:50.416 --> 32:53.416
I said-- I just said that I saw a samurai

32:53.500 --> 32:55.208
walking with a girl--

32:55.291 --> 32:56.375
[screams]

33:00.250 --> 33:01.708
Kokushu,

33:02.375 --> 33:04.833
this time I won't let you get away.

33:15.000 --> 33:16.916
[dramatic music fades]

33:24.916 --> 33:27.833
All right.
I suppose this is where we split.

33:27.916 --> 33:28.833
What?

33:28.916 --> 33:31.458
Shinnosuke and I made quite a mess
at the police station.

33:31.541 --> 33:34.541
They've seen our faces.
We're likely wanted men now.

33:34.625 --> 33:35.458
Huh?

33:36.083 --> 33:37.208
So I'm thinking

33:37.291 --> 33:39.875
we split into two groups for now,
until things cool down.

33:39.958 --> 33:41.250
Will the two of you be all right?

33:41.333 --> 33:43.041
Have you forgotten
who you're dealing with?

33:43.125 --> 33:44.416
You watch your own back.

33:44.500 --> 33:46.000
Till we meet again.

33:47.416 --> 33:49.041
Come on, Shinnosuke!

33:49.750 --> 33:50.666
Uh…

33:51.250 --> 33:52.666
W-- Wait for me, Kyojin!

33:54.791 --> 33:55.916
Let's get moving.

34:03.333 --> 34:05.500
[mysterious music playing]

34:05.583 --> 34:06.500
[exhales]

34:12.041 --> 34:13.333
[inhales sharply]

34:13.416 --> 34:14.416
[sighs]

34:16.500 --> 34:18.125
[owl hooting]

34:20.583 --> 34:21.458
[sighs]

34:22.041 --> 34:23.125
[groans]

34:26.708 --> 34:28.208
[suspenseful music playing]

34:36.333 --> 34:38.333
EUROPEAN CIPHER MANUAL

34:38.416 --> 34:40.083
[Okubo] The Bureau was his doing.

34:40.166 --> 34:42.833
Kawaji went overseas
to develop a plan for it,

34:42.916 --> 34:45.333
went to Europe
to learn new ideas for law and order.

34:53.833 --> 34:54.833
[inhales]

34:59.750 --> 35:00.791
N, K…

35:02.458 --> 35:05.458
W, D, A…

35:05.541 --> 35:09.791
Z is W. Another A…

35:10.625 --> 35:11.625
I…

35:28.125 --> 35:29.166
[panting]

35:38.875 --> 35:40.208
[wheezing]

35:40.291 --> 35:43.083
-[gasps]
-[suspenseful music fades]

35:48.208 --> 35:50.583
[Enju] Lord Shinpei. Good evening.

35:53.750 --> 35:55.291
[Nagase] Mochizuki.

35:55.375 --> 35:58.041
What brings someone from the Police Bureau
to the Home Ministry?

35:58.625 --> 36:00.541
Especially at this hour of the night?

36:01.041 --> 36:02.666
It is late, indeed.

36:03.416 --> 36:04.708
Are you still working?

36:04.791 --> 36:05.916
[eerie music playing]

36:06.000 --> 36:07.375
[breathing shakily]

36:09.791 --> 36:12.041
Don't tell me you underestimated us.

36:13.375 --> 36:16.166
You must have realized
we'd be watching every move.

36:19.041 --> 36:20.500
What is the purpose of this anyway?

36:20.583 --> 36:22.375
That's none of your business, is it?

36:26.333 --> 36:28.166
You were just a few steps away.

36:28.250 --> 36:29.583
So close.

36:30.166 --> 36:31.833
How unfortunate.

36:33.166 --> 36:34.000
[gasps]

36:34.083 --> 36:35.083
[choking]

36:35.708 --> 36:37.458
[dramatic music playing]

36:49.750 --> 36:53.250
REPORT TO KAWAJI
SAKURA AND SHUJIRO FACE-TO-FACE

36:53.333 --> 36:54.916
[eerie music playing]

36:55.000 --> 36:56.583
[clock ticking]

37:00.125 --> 37:01.208
[owl hooting]

37:04.750 --> 37:07.833
TO TOSHIYOSHI KAWAJI

37:09.708 --> 37:10.708
[exhales]

37:13.166 --> 37:15.791
Looks like there won't be
any more developments today.

37:15.875 --> 37:17.708
I'd say we retire for the night.

37:17.791 --> 37:20.208
Right. Gentlemen,

37:20.291 --> 37:22.750
rest well tonight
in the comfort of your rooms.

37:22.833 --> 37:26.041
If all goes well, the results
from Chiryu will arrive by morning.

37:26.125 --> 37:28.375
[Morosawa] Well then,
see you all tomorrow.

37:30.333 --> 37:32.541
[men speaking indistinctly]

37:32.625 --> 37:35.000
Okubo's secretary has been
dealt with smoothly.

37:35.083 --> 37:35.916
Very good.

37:36.000 --> 37:39.750
Even so, tensions are rising
at the central government, sir.

37:40.958 --> 37:44.958
Maejima has suddenly changed his plans
and is now bound for Okazaki.

37:45.041 --> 37:47.333
We've found evidence
of telegram communications

37:47.416 --> 37:49.666
with one of the Kodoku participants.

37:50.166 --> 37:51.250
And do we know who it is?

37:51.333 --> 37:53.000
One hundred and eight, Saga Shujiro.

37:53.083 --> 37:54.625
[footsteps receding]

37:59.500 --> 38:00.666
[Kawaji] Pardon me.

38:01.375 --> 38:04.833
Gentlemen, there has been
a slight complication, I'm afraid.

38:07.000 --> 38:10.666
Unfortunately, Lord Okubo is likely aware

38:10.750 --> 38:13.041
of your involvement
alongside the Police Bureau.

38:13.125 --> 38:14.166
[gasping]

38:15.458 --> 38:17.041
What do you mean by that?

38:17.125 --> 38:19.291
If-- If that's the case,
our standing might be--

38:19.375 --> 38:21.250
Please rest assured.

38:21.333 --> 38:24.083
This is going exactly as we've foreseen.

38:24.166 --> 38:26.500
I have everything thoroughly planned out.

38:26.583 --> 38:28.916
How on earth
could they figure out who we are?

38:29.666 --> 38:34.791
Apparently, Maejima received a telegram
from one of the contestants with the news.

38:34.875 --> 38:37.583
Wait, what?
Is-- Isn't that against the rules?

38:37.666 --> 38:39.791
The telegram was from Saga Shujiro.

38:39.875 --> 38:41.416
Kokushu the Manslayer.

38:41.500 --> 38:43.833
Wait. Is he eliminated for that?

38:43.916 --> 38:45.666
[Kawaji] I'm afraid
that won't be the case.

38:45.750 --> 38:48.750
-Why not? I don't understand--
-Calm yourselves. Easy.

38:50.000 --> 38:51.833
We have received word

38:51.916 --> 38:55.083
that one or more intriguing
and ruthless participants are rather

38:55.166 --> 38:57.000
fixated on Saga Shujiro.

38:57.083 --> 38:59.166
[brooding music playing]

39:00.208 --> 39:02.166
Why would we interfere,

39:03.041 --> 39:05.750
when we can witness these lost souls

39:05.833 --> 39:08.708
tear each other apart
inside the Kodoku jar?

39:13.958 --> 39:16.416
-[drum beating]
-[indistinct chatter]

39:16.500 --> 39:18.125
[children singing]

39:27.583 --> 39:28.833
A festival…

39:31.875 --> 39:35.666
[man] How about a mask, folks?
[speaks indistinctly]

39:35.750 --> 39:37.375
Take your pick!

39:38.250 --> 39:40.500
Come and get your masks!

39:40.583 --> 39:42.083
[folk music playing]

39:46.750 --> 39:48.375
[ominous music playing]

39:49.375 --> 39:52.666
[Kyojin] Got a moment to chat,
Gion Sansuke?

39:54.000 --> 39:55.125
How do you know me?

39:55.208 --> 39:57.458
Well, I don't, really.

39:58.458 --> 39:59.750
[grunting]

40:02.500 --> 40:05.208
I've got no intention of fighting,

40:05.291 --> 40:07.000
Adashino Shikura.

40:07.916 --> 40:08.916
[exhales]

40:09.000 --> 40:10.750
[dramatic music playing]

40:12.833 --> 40:16.000
If I'm not wrong,
you two are looking for your siblings,

40:17.875 --> 40:20.791
Saga Shujiro and Kinugasa Iroha.

40:21.791 --> 40:24.208
Oh, and then there's Jinroku too, right?

40:24.291 --> 40:25.958
What exactly is it that you want?

40:27.666 --> 40:28.916
I wonder

40:29.458 --> 40:32.708
would either of you care
if your siblings were in trouble?

40:46.541 --> 40:49.500
-Uh, excuse me. Which way is Chiryu?
-[music ends abruptly]

40:49.583 --> 40:51.416
-Pardon me?
-I think I took a wrong turn.

40:51.500 --> 40:52.750
[dramatic music resumes]

41:01.833 --> 41:02.958
What are you talking about?

41:20.083 --> 41:22.708
63 REMAINING

41:22.791 --> 41:24.875
[dramatic music fades]

41:24.958 --> 41:26.833
[ambient music playing]

45:15.333 --> 45:16.500
[music fades]
